EOF
Deliverable: vars/manage-config.yml created and valid YAML.

Subtask 3.2: Create the Health-Check and Capacity-Reporting Playbook
This playbook queries the live StorageCluster and CephCluster status fields that ODF actually populates, and reports on operator pod health, StorageCluster phase, and Ceph cluster health state.

cat > playbooks/manage-odf.yml << 'EOF'
---
- name: Comprehensive ODF Management
  hosts: localhost
  gather_facts: false
  vars_files:
    - ../vars/odf-config.yml
    - ../vars/manage-config.yml

  tasks:
    - name: Check ODF cluster health via StorageCluster status
      kubernetes.core.k8s_info:
        api_version: ocs.openshift.io/v1
        kind: StorageCluster
        name: "{{ storage_cluster_name }}"
        namespace: "{{ odf_namespace }}"
      register: storage_cluster_health

    - name: Report StorageCluster phase
      debug:
        msg: "StorageCluster {{ storage_cluster_name }} phase: {{ storage_cluster_health.resources[0].status.phase | default('Unknown') }}"
      when: storage_cluster_health.resources | length > 0

    - name: Fail fast if StorageCluster is not found
      debug:
        msg: "WARNING: StorageCluster {{ storage_cluster_name }} not found in namespace {{ odf_namespace }}. Skipping remaining checks."
      when: storage_cluster_health.resources | length == 0

    - name: Check underlying CephCluster health
      kubernetes.core.k8s_info:
        api_version: ceph.rook.io/v1
        kind: CephCluster
        namespace: "{{ odf_namespace }}"
      register: ceph_cluster_health
      when: storage_cluster_health.resources | length > 0

    - name: Report CephCluster health state
      debug:
        msg: "CephCluster {{ item.metadata.name }} health: {{ item.status.ceph.health | default('Unknown') }}"
      loop: "{{ ceph_cluster_health.resources }}"
      when:
        - storage_cluster_health.resources | length > 0
        - ceph_cluster_health.resources is defined

    - name: List pods in the ODF namespace
      kubernetes.core.k8s_info:
        api_version: v1
        kind: Pod
        namespace: "{{ odf_namespace }}"
      register: odf_pods

    - name: Report any pods not in Running or Succeeded phase
      debug:
        msg: "Pod {{ item.metadata.name }} is in phase {{ item.status.phase }}"
      loop: "{{ odf_pods.resources }}"
      when: item.status.phase not in ['Running', 'Succeeded']

    - name: Count total pods versus running pods
      debug:
        msg: "ODF namespace has {{ odf_pods.resources | length }} pods total, {{ odf_pods.resources | selectattr('status.phase', 'equalto', 'Running') | list | length }} in Running phase"
EOF
Deliverable: playbooks/manage-odf.yml is complete and passes:

ansible-playbook playbooks/manage-odf.yml --syntax-check
If run against a live cluster (ansible-playbook playbooks/manage-odf.yml -v), expect debug output showing the StorageCluster phase (typically Ready), the CephCluster health string (typically HEALTH_OK), and a final pod count summary such as ODF namespace has 24 pods total, 24 in Running phase.

